    "narrative": "For June 23, 2026, **Cal Raleigh** headlines our starts with a 68.07 efficiency score, benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against M. Keller and a +11% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile. He is closely chased by **Luis Arraez** (66.78) and **Matt Chapman** (66.58), both of whom capitalize on a soft matchup against Aaron Civale. While **Luis Arraez** carries some BvP risk, his role at the top of the order and positive wind conditions outweigh the noise. **Jonathan Aranda** is another high-floor play at 63.49; his dynamic platoon edge (+12%) against Avila and strong xwOBA of .376 make him a superior utility option compared to the more volatile profiles on our bench.\n\nThe optimizer\u2019s toughest exclusion today was **Geraldo Perdomo**, who finished with a 55.34 score, just missing the cut behind **Masyn Winn**. While **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s efficiency is solid, **Masyn Winn** edged him out due to the potential for stolen bases\u2014a critical priority for LawDog\u2014coupled with a favorable matchup against the left-handed E. Rodriguez. Note that several lineup slots, including **Luis Arraez**, **Matt Chapman**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Taylor Ward**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Jeremiah Jackson**, are based on projected batting orders; any mid-day shuffling in these lineups could fluctuate these efficiency scores. We remain cautious with **Jeremiah Jackson** (56.58), whose efficiency is suppressed by a bottom-of-the-order assignment and a difficult opposing catcher, but his presence remains necessary to balance our overall team velocity requirements.",
